---
layout: base
pagination:
  data: glazePages
  size: 1
  alias: glaze
  # Without this only the first of the generated pages lands in
  # collections.all, and the sitemap would list one glaze instead of all
  # of them -- on pages built to be found in search, that is the whole
  # point missed.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ glaze.path }}"
eleventyComputed:
  # "Jericho" alone means nothing in a search result, "Jericho glaze" does.
  # safe, in both: the SEO plugin escapes what it writes into the head. Without
  # it the apostrophe in "I don't revisit it often" was escaped twice and
  # reached the search snippet as "don&#39;t".
  title: "{{ glaze.name | safe }} glaze"
  # eleventy-plugin-seo reads "excerpt" as the page description (ADR 0002).
  excerpt: "{{ glaze.lead | safe }}"
---
{# One page per glaze, generated from the gallery entries (see
   _data/glazePages.js). The page stays in the site's own palette: paper,
   white and blue. The glaze colour appears only as the dot beside the name,
   the way it does on the cards — a band in the glaze colour would drag
   sixteen foreign colours into the design.

   Order follows what the numbers showed: the pieces sell, so they come
   early, under the full description. A second text block below the pieces
   was tried and dropped — with the same headings on sixteen pages it would
   read as filler. The lead stays a separate field only because the search
   snippet needs two sentences, not the whole text. #}
<article>
    {# The glaze and its picture open the page together: name and text on the
       left, the group photo on the right. Someone arriving from a search has
       not seen the card yet, so the page shows what the glaze looks like
       before it says anything else. The photo keeps its 4:3 on every page --
       it used to stretch to the height of the tiles beside it, which gave it
       a different crop on all sixteen and cut teapots off at the spout.

       The picture is Matthew's group photo where he has taken one and the
       glaze's own card otherwise. #}
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-12">
        {% set shopUrl = (global.shop.base + global.shop.collectionsPath + "/" + glaze.slug) | shopLink("glaze-" + glaze.name + "-shop") %}
        {# Three parts: name, photo, text. On a phone they stand in that order,
           so the photo comes right after the name and not below a screenful
           of text -- it used to start at 631 of 812 pixels. From md up the
           photo takes the right column over both rows, and the two text parts
           meet in the middle of the left one: the name sits at the bottom of
           its row, the text at the top of the next, and the free height is
           shared evenly above and below. #}
        <div class="grid gap-x-10 gap-y-6 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-y-0 lg:gap-x-12">
            <div class="md:self-end">
                {# Label and heading as on every other page of the site: blue label, ink heading, mt-3 between them (collections, events, about, the home hero). #}
                <p class="cap-label text-blue">{{ collections_glaze.eyebrow }}{% if glaze.group %} &middot; {{ glaze.group }}{% endif %}</p>
                <h1 class="mt-3 flex items-start gap-3.5 font-display text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-ink">
                    {# The dot that stands beside a glaze's name everywhere on the site, here large enough to read as a sample of the colour. No ring around it: it pushed the dot five pixels out past the left edge the label and the text share, and the palest glaze stands off the paper without one. It stands at the first line (mt-2 centres 30px in a 45px line), so a name that wraps -- Squamish Nights on a phone -- does not leave it hanging between two lines. A marker stroke in the glaze colour was tried here and dropped -- the heading is not a link, and at half strength the colours went dull, the charcoals to a grey bar. #}
                    <span class="mt-2 h-7.5 w-7.5 flex-none rounded-full" style="background-color: {{ glaze.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{ glaze.name }}
                </h1>
                {# The card's one-liner under the name, as a sentence in the display serif: the second voice of the page between the heavy name and the grey text. It was blue capitals first, the way the featured piece on the home page carries its caption, but a line this long (Skaha's runs to eighty characters) is three rows of capitals and reads as a block, not as a caption. Ink, not blue: blue is the colour of labels and links here. #}
                {% if glaze.text %}<p class="mt-3 text-balance font-display text-lg font-medium leading-7 text-ink md:text-xl">{{ glaze.text | trim | replace(r/\.$/, "") }}.</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {# Das erste Bild der Seite und meist ihr größtes: Es lädt sofort,
               nicht erst beim Scrollen. Ein Link ist es nur, solange es in
               der Sammlung dahinter etwas zu kaufen gibt (glaze.available). #}
            {% if glaze.available %}
            <a href="{{ (global.shop.base + global.shop.collectionsPath + "/" + glaze.slug) | shopLink("glaze-" + glaze.name + "-feature") }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="group relative block aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden bg-tile md:col-start-2 md:row-span-2 md:row-start-1 md:self-center">
                {% img glaze.feature.url, glaze.feature.alt, "(min-width: 1152px) 528px, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw", "img-zoom absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover", "eager" %}
            </a>
            {% else %}
            <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden bg-tile md:col-start-2 md:row-span-2 md:row-start-1 md:self-center">
                {% img glaze.feature.url, glaze.feature.alt, "(min-width: 1152px) 528px, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw", "absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover", "eager" %}
            </div>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="md:self-start">
                {# text-pretty keeps a paragraph from ending on one stranded word ("... design traits around / Yaletown."), text-balance evens out a tagline that runs to two lines. Paragraphs stand 16px apart, the same step as between tagline and text: at 12px, under half a line of this type, they read as one block. #}
                <p class="text-pretty text-base leading-relaxed text-muted md:mt-4">{{ glaze.lead }}</p>
                {% for paragraph in glaze.paragraphs %}
                <p class="mt-4 text-pretty text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ paragraph }}</p>
                {% endfor %}
                {# Ohne verfügbare Stücke führte der Knopf auf eine leere
                   Sammlung im Shop oder auf eine, in der alles ausverkauft
                   ist (Dogwood: vier von vier). Hinaus führt dort die
                   Marktkachel weiter unten. #}
                {% if glaze.available %}<a href="{{ shopUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary mt-6">{{ collections_glaze.shop_cta_all | replace("{glaze}", glaze.name) }}</a>{% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# The pieces of this glaze, as a slider. They come from the shop, not
       from the CMS: a list typed in once was stale two months later, with
       fifteen of twenty tiles sold out while the shop held fifty-seven pieces
       (ADR 0006). Every piece that can be bought is here; sold-out ones only
       fill up to four (see _data/glazePages.js). #}
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12" aria-label="This glaze in the shop">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-black text-ink">{{ collections_glaze.pieces_title | replace("{glaze}", glaze.name) }}</h2>
            {# Der Weg in den ganzen Shop, auf allen sechzehn Seiten gleich. Der
               Weg zu den Stücken dieser Glasur ist der Knopf im Kopf. #}
            <a href="{{ (global.shop.base + global.shop.collectionsPath + "/") | shopLink("glaze-" + glaze.name + "-shop-all") }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-underline whitespace-nowrap text-sm">{{ collections_glaze.shop_all_label }}</a>
        </div>
        {# Die Reihe hat eine feste Folge: erst die Stücke, am Ende immer die
           Marktkachel und der nächste Markt. Sind das zusammen weniger als
           vier Karten, stehen dazwischen Platzhalter -- so ist die erste
           Ansicht auch bei einer Glasur ohne Stücke voll, und die Reihe
           läuft sichtbar weiter.

           Vorher war die Reihe ein Raster mit vier Plätzen, und was die
           Stücke frei ließen, bekamen Marktkachel, Termin und Platzhalter.
           Das brauchte für Telefon, Tablet und Schreibtisch je eine eigene
           Regel und zeigte nie mehr als vier Stücke, auch wenn der Shop zwölf
           verfügbare hielt. #}
        {% set upcoming = events | occurrences | filterUpcoming | byDateAsc %}
        {% set shortlist = upcoming | nextUp %}
        {% set platzhalter = 2 - glaze.pieces.length %}
        {% if platzhalter < 0 %}{% set platzhalter = 0 %}{% endif %}
        {# With two pieces or fewer the row holds exactly four cards, and they
           simply stand there: four in a row from lg up, two by two below. A
           slider with nothing to slide would only be a row that can be
           nudged. From three pieces on there are more cards than fit, and
           the row becomes a slider. #}
        {% set alsSlider = glaze.pieces.length > 2 %}
        {# As a slider the row shows four cards to a view from lg up and two
           below, and in both a strip of the next one at the right edge. At
           exactly a quarter each, four pixels of the fifth were left and
           nothing said that the row goes on; 22.5% leaves some fifty. Every
           card that is not a piece is a square like the photos and ends on
           their lower edge. #}
        {% set karte = "w-[45%] flex-none snap-start lg:w-[22.5%]" if alsSlider else "" %}
        {# data-slider: home-slider.js gives this row the line and the arrows
           below it (slider-nav.njk). "still" keeps it from advancing on its
           own the way the glaze sliders do: someone reading prices should
           not have the row pulled away. data-slots: events.js keeps one date visible and
           lets the next one move up when it has passed. #}
        <div id="glaze-markets"{% if alsSlider %} data-slider="still"{% endif %} data-slots="1" class="mt-8 {% if alsSlider %}no-scrollbar -mx-6 flex snap-x snap-mandatory items-start gap-5 overflow-x-auto scroll-px-6 px-6 pb-2{% else %}grid grid-cols-2 items-start gap-5 lg:grid-cols-4{% endif %}">
            {% for piece in glaze.pieces %}
            <a href="{{ piece.url | shopLink("glaze-" + glaze.name + "-tile" + loop.index) }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="group {{ karte }}">
                {# The square belongs to the frame, not to the image: a piece
                   the shop lists without a photo keeps its place in the row. #}
                <div class="relative aspect-square overflow-hidden bg-white">
                    {# The shop says in the same answer whether a piece is to
                       be had, so no second request is needed for the label. #}
                    {% if not piece.available %}<span class="cap-label absolute right-2 top-2 z-10 bg-sand px-2 py-1 font-bold text-ink">{{ global.labels.sold_out | default("Sold out", true) }}</span>{% endif %}
                    {# sizes: the widest a card gets -- a quarter of the row without the slider, a little less with it. #}
                    {% img piece.image, piece.alt, "(min-width: 1152px) 264px, (min-width: 1024px) 25vw, 50vw", "img-zoom h-full w-full object-contain", "lazy", true %}
                </div>
                <div class="mt-2 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                    {# Always two lines high: "Medium Teapot - Yaletown Red" wraps, "Shorty Mug" does not, and a row whose captions end at different heights reads as restless. A third line is cut. #}
                    <p class="line-clamp-2 min-h-10 font-display text-sm font-black text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-blue">{{ piece.title | withoutGlaze(glaze.name) }}</p>
                    {% if piece.price %}<p class="flex-none text-sm font-medium text-muted">{{ piece.price }}</p>{% endif %}
                </div>
            </a>
            {% endfor %}

            {# The empty places are built like a piece: a white square like the
               ground of the product photos, and a line of text below it where
               a piece carries its name. In the square stand three dogwood
               flowers in the glaze colour -- the flower from under the heading
               of the collections page -- each paler than the one before, the
               way three dots trail off: more is on its way. One flower alone
               only marked the spot and left the saying to the text. A fine line inside the edge was tried and read as a
               frame around nothing. The line below says what to expect,
               in the type of the piece names; its line break comes from the
               CMS (whitespace-pre-line), and two lines are what a name takes.

               Tried before: a field of glaze colour with a pale X, which
               outweighed the photos beside it, and the text in place of the
               flower under the pointer, which a phone never showed. They say
               nothing a screen reader needs: the market tile says the same in
               a sentence. #}
            {% for n in range(0, platzhalter) %}
            {# Two of them side by side, with the same flowers and the same
               line, looked like one tile printed twice. So the flowers fade
               across both as one row of six, and the line stands under the
               first only. #}
            {% set stufen = ["", "opacity-45", "opacity-20"] %}
            {% if platzhalter > 1 %}{% set stufen = ["", "opacity-60", "opacity-35"] if n == 0 else ["opacity-20", "opacity-10", "opacity-5"] %}{% endif %}
            <div class="{{ karte }}" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="relative flex aspect-square items-center justify-center bg-white" style="color: {{ glaze.swatch }}">
                    <span class="flex w-[62%] items-center justify-between [&>span]:w-[28%] [&_svg]:h-auto [&_svg]:w-full">
                        {% for stufe in stufen %}<span class="{{ stufe }}">{% include "dogwood.njk" %}</span>{% endfor %}
                    </span>
                </div>
                {% if collections_glaze.empty_note and n == 0 %}<p class="mt-2 min-h-10 whitespace-pre-line font-display text-sm font-black text-ink">{{ collections_glaze.empty_note }}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% endfor %}

            {# Der blaue Rahmen trennt sie von den Stücken daneben, die
               keinen haben. Dieselbe Markierung trägt auf der Events-Seite
               der nächste Termin.

               Der erste Satz gilt bei leerem wie bei vollem Shop. Eine
               Entschuldigung ("Sorry, not much ... in the shop") stand hier
               zuerst und passte nicht mehr, seit die Kachel auch neben zwölf
               Stücken steht; zwei Sätze je nach Bestand waren ein Feld mehr,
               als die Aussage braucht. Der zweite Satz entfällt, wo die
               Kachel für ihn zu schmal
               ist: auf dem Telefon (rund 155 Pixel) und von lg bis 1151 Pixel
               (rund 220). Ab 1152 hat die Seite ihre volle Breite (max-w-6xl)
               und die Kachel 248 Pixel; xl wäre mit 1280 zu spät gewesen. Auf
               dem Telefon steht auch die Linkzeile nicht -- die ganze Kachel
               führt zu den Terminen.

               Steht kein Termin neben ihr, nimmt die Kachel dessen Platz mit
               ein (main.css, [data-market-tile]).

               Ohne Termin stimmt der Satz über die Märkte nicht mehr, also
               steht dort dieselbe Zeile wie im Terminband. events.js tauscht
               sie, wenn der letzte Termin vorbeigezogen ist, seit die Seite
               gebaut wurde. #}
            {# The glaze name stands out the way a glaze does in the blurbs on the home page: .text-highlight, blue in its light variant (.blurb-inline). #}
            {# Auf dem Telefon misst eine Karte 130 bis 155 Pixel. In ein Quadrat
               dieser Größe passen Satz und Marktname nur in 12 Pixel Schrift,
               und die war zu klein. Dort sind Marktkachel und Termin deshalb
               keine Quadrate, sondern so hoch, wie ihr Text in lesbarer Größe
               braucht (max-sm:aspect-auto und self-stretch); die Karten der
               Reihe strecken sich gemeinsam. Ab sm sind es wieder Quadrate. #}
            {# The type follows the card, not the screen. A card is widest on a
               tablet, where two share the row (some 350 pixels from md up),
               and narrower again from lg, where four do (220 to 260). So the
               sizes go up at md and back down at lg -- with one size from sm
               up, the tablet card stood half empty under small type. #}
            {% set glasurname = '<span class="text-highlight font-bold">' ~ (glaze.name | escape) ~ '</span>' %}
            <a href="/events.html" data-market-tile class="group flex aspect-square flex-col rounded-xl border-2 border-blue bg-white p-3 max-sm:aspect-auto max-sm:self-stretch sm:p-5 lg:p-4 {{ karte }}">
                <p class="font-display text-base font-black leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-blue sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-lg min-[1152px]:text-xl">{{ collections_glaze.market_title | replace("{glaze}", glaze.name) }}</p>
                <p data-market-text class="blurb-inline mt-1.5 text-sm leading-snug text-muted sm:mt-2 sm:leading-relaxed md:text-base lg:text-sm"{% if not shortlist.length %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ collections_glaze.market_text | escape | replace("{glaze}", glasurname) | safe }}{% if collections_glaze.market_text_more %}<span class="max-sm:hidden lg:max-[1151px]:hidden"> {{ collections_glaze.market_text_more }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
                <p data-market-soon class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-snug text-muted sm:mt-2 sm:leading-relaxed md:text-base lg:text-sm"{% if shortlist.length %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ global.labels.dates_soon }}</p>
                <span class="link-underline mt-auto inline-block self-start pt-4 text-sm max-sm:hidden md:text-base lg:text-sm">{{ collections_glaze.market_cta }}</span>
            </a>

            {# Wie im Terminband steht jeder kommende Termin im HTML, und nur
               der erste ist sichtbar: events.js wiederholt die Auswahl im
               Browser, damit ein Markt verschwindet, der seit dem Bau vorbei
               ist. Beim Überfahren wird die Haarlinie blau und der Name auch --
               so reagieren weiße Flächen auf dieser Seite überall (Kartenknopf,
               Formularfelder). Eine andere Flächenfarbe gibt es nur im blauen
               Terminband. Ort und Uhrzeit stehen ab sm; auf dem Telefon hält
               die Kachel nur Tag und Markt. #}
            {% for event in upcoming %}
            {% set rank = shortlist.indexOf(event) %}
            <a href="/events.html"
               data-event
               data-date="{{ event.date | date('yyyy-MM-dd') }}"
               data-until="{{ (event.end_date or event.date) | date('yyyy-MM-dd') }}"
               data-name="{{ event.name | trim }}"
               {% if rank != 0 %}hidden{% endif %}
               class="group flex aspect-square flex-col rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-white p-3 transition-colors hover:border-blue max-sm:aspect-auto max-sm:self-stretch sm:p-5 lg:p-4 {{ karte }}">
                <p data-next-label class="cap-label mb-1 text-blue sm:mb-2"{% if rank != 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ global.labels.next_up }}</p>
                <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
                    <span class="font-display text-2xl font-black text-ink sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-3xl">{{ event.date | date("d") }}</span>
                    <span class="cap-label text-muted">{{ event.date | date("MMM") }}</span>
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 font-display text-base font-black leading-snug text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-blue sm:mt-3 md:text-xl lg:text-base">{{ event.name }}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted max-sm:hidden md:text-base lg:text-sm">{{ event.location }}</p>
                {% if event.time %}<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted max-sm:hidden md:text-base lg:text-sm">{{ event.time }}</p>{% endif %}
            </a>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% if alsSlider %}{% set sliderZiel = "glaze-markets" %}{% include "slider-nav.njk" %}{% endif %}
        {# Same line the home page carries under the same pieces: every tile
           here leaves the site, and saying so once under the block is friendlier
           than finding out at the checkout. #}
        {% if collections_glaze.pieces_note and glaze.pieces.length %}<p class="mt-6 text-center text-xs text-muted">{{ collections_glaze.pieces_note }}</p>{% endif %}
        {# Dieselbe Datei wie im Terminband: Sie entfernt Termine, die seit
           dem Bau vorbei sind, und zieht die dahinter nach. #}
        <script defer src="/js/events.js"></script>
    </section>

    {# Half the tiles can be sold out at any time, and the shop never holds
       everything Matthew has made. Without this the page is a dead end for
       exactly the visitor who wants this glaze most. Wording follows his own
       answers in the FAQ.

       Blue, because on this site blue is the colour of Matthew speaking for
       himself: the events band and the About teaser are the only other two,
       and both are on the home page. This block is him in the first person,
       so it belongs with those and not with the paper and white the shop
       content uses. It also catches the dark bottom edge of the photo above,
       which a white band collided with. #}
    <section class="bg-blue">
        <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl md:grid-cols-2">
            {# One picture for all sixteen bands: a teapot lifted out of the
               kiln, more pots still standing inside. The text beside it offers
               to make a piece, and the picture shows the making -- a product
               shot of one finished piece would read as "this one", not as
               "yours next". A per-glaze photo was tried and dropped: on two
               pages it showed a glazed piece under "not in the shop right
               now", and the card image must never appear here at all, because
               the visitor clicked on it to get here. The picture comes from
               Collections - Glaze page in the CMS. #}
            <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden md:aspect-auto">
                {% img collections_glaze.ask_image.url, collections_glaze.ask_image.alt, "(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw", "absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" %}
            </div>
            {# Same shape as the About teaser on the home page (story-teaser.njk):
               label, heading, text, action, on the same spacing. Both are
               Matthew speaking in blue, and two blue bands built differently
               would read as two different kinds of thing. #}
            <div class="flex flex-col items-start justify-center px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-14">
                {% if collections_glaze.ask_eyebrow %}<p class="cap-label text-sand">{{ collections_glaze.ask_eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
                <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-black leading-tight text-paper">{{ collections_glaze.ask_title }}</h2>
                {# The glaze name stands out here as it does in the market tile above: .text-highlight, which is sand on a dark ground. #}
                <p class="mt-4 max-w-md text-base leading-relaxed text-paper/80">{{ collections_glaze.ask_text | escape | replace("{glaze}", '<span class="text-highlight font-bold">' ~ (glaze.name | escape) ~ '</span>') | safe }}</p>
                <a href="/contact.html" class="link-underline link-invert mt-8 inline-block text-sm">{{ collections_glaze.ask_cta | replace("{glaze}", glaze.name) }}</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# The page we want people to keep circling back to, so the other glazes
       get cards here, not a thin row of links. It is the slider from the home
       page (home-slider.js looks for #glaze-slider): all fifteen other glazes
       can be reached from here, where a grid of four showed the next four and
       hid the rest. The strip of dots the home page carries under it is left
       out -- with it the foot of the page was a second navigation, and the
       way back to all glazes stands beside the heading instead. The order starts
       with the glaze after this one, see _data/glazePages.js. #}
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12" aria-label="Other glazes">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
            <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-black text-ink">{{ collections_glaze.others_title }}</h2>
            <a href="/collections.html" class="link-underline whitespace-nowrap text-sm">{{ collections_glaze.back_label | glazeCount(gallery.items.length) }}</a>
        </div>
        <div id="glaze-slider" class="no-scrollbar -mx-6 mt-8 flex snap-x snap-mandatory gap-5 overflow-x-auto scroll-px-6 px-6 pb-2">
            {% for other in glaze.others %}
            <a href="{{ other.path }}" class="group w-[86%] flex-none snap-start sm:w-[45%] md:w-[31%]">
                <div class="aspect-[4/3] w-full overflow-hidden" style="background-color: {{ other.swatch }}">
                    {% img other.image.url, other.image.alt, "(min-width: 1152px) 342px, (min-width: 768px) 31vw, 86vw", "img-zoom h-full w-full object-cover" %}
                </div>
                <p class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-2 font-display text-base font-black text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-blue">
                    <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 flex-none rounded-full" style="background-color: {{ other.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    {{ other.name }}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">{{ other.text }}</p>
            </a>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {# No colour dots here, so the line and the arrows take their place. #}
        {% set sliderZiel = "glaze-slider" %}{% include "slider-nav.njk" %}
        <script defer src="/js/home-slider.js"></script>
    </section>
</article>
